        "id": 25824,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-01-29T19:46:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>First, immunity is immunity, period.  If not, then it could easily be contrived that “Oh, the immunity was applied first, so 0 damage, but then the +1 modifier means I still hit him for a point of damage.”  Second, Christopher has stated that if an attack results in zero or fewer points of damage, the attack is then canceled, and thus there is no damage, and no responses to damage.</p>\n<p>That said, Ra and Absolute Zero can have their moments, given almost any other situation.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
